-- Independent tests of the ePrivacy Directive encoding. Expected values were decided from the text alone in ANSWERS.md, before any module was opened.
-- Each #ASSERT is one line: scenario number, provision, the facts, and the convention sentence relied on where the expected value rests on it.
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered.

#ASSERT (`Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` WITH `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 1. Art 1(3): Guide: flat negative "shall not apply"
#ASSERT (`Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` WITH `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS TRUE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 2. Art 1(3): Guide: flat negative "shall not apply"
#ASSERT (`Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` WITH `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS TRUE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 3. Art 1(3): Guide: flat negative "shall not apply"
#ASSERT (`Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` WITH `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS TRUE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 4. Art 1(3): Guide: flat negative "shall not apply"
#ASSERT (`Art 1(3) the Directive applies to the activity` WITH `the activity falls outside the scope of the Treaty establishing the European Community` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns public security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns defence` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns State security` IS FALSE, `the activity concerns the economic well-being of the State` IS FALSE, `the activity relates to State security matters` IS FALSE, `the activity is an activity of the State in areas of criminal law` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 5. Art 1(3): Guide: exclusion is not closed with only; ordinary commercial activity not named, silent
#ASSERT (`Art 2(a) the person is a user` WITH `the person is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 6. Art 2(a): business purposes, never subscribed: neither is a condition
#ASSERT (`Art 2(a) the person is a user` WITH `the person is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 7. Art 2(a): private purposes, subscribed
#ASSERT (`Art 2(a) the person is a user` WITH `the person is a natural person` IS FALSE, `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 8. Art 2(a): Guide: means definition; a company is not a natural person
#ASSERT (`Art 2(a) the person is a user` WITH `the person is a natural person` IS TRUE, `the person uses a publicly available electronic communications service` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 9. Art 2(a): Guide: means definition; private network is not a publicly available service
#ASSERT (`Art 2(b) the data is traffic data` WITH `the data is processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network` IS FALSE, `the data is processed for the billing of a communication` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 10. Art 2(b)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(b) the data is traffic data` WITH `the data is processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network` IS TRUE, `the data is processed for the billing of a communication` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 11. Art 2(b)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(b) the data is traffic data` WITH `the data is processed for the purpose of the conveyance of a communication on an electronic communications network` IS FALSE, `the data is processed for the billing of a communication` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 12. Art 2(b): Guide: means definition; advertising profile only
#ASSERT (`Art 2(c) the data is location data` WITH `the data is processed in an electronic communications network` IS TRUE, `the data is processed by an electronic communications service` IS FALSE, `the data indicates the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 13. Art 2(c)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(c) the data is location data` WITH `the data is processed in an electronic communications network` IS FALSE, `the data is processed by an electronic communications service` IS FALSE, `the data indicates the geographic position of the terminal equipment of a user of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 14. Art 2(c): Guide: means definition; held only on the handset, not processed in a network or by a service
#ASSERT (`Art 2(d) the information is a communication` WITH `the information is exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties` IS TRUE, `the information is exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 15. Art 2(d)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(d) second sentence the information is a communication` WITH `the information is conveyed as part of a broadcasting service to the public over an electronic communications network` IS TRUE, `the information can be related to the identifiable subscriber or user receiving it` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 16. Art 2(d) second sentence: broadcast not relatable to an identifiable subscriber
#ASSERT (`Art 2(d) second sentence the information is a communication` WITH `the information is conveyed as part of a broadcasting service to the public over an electronic communications network` IS TRUE, `the information can be related to the identifiable subscriber or user receiving it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 17. Art 2(d) second sentence: broadcast-service stream relatable to one identifiable subscriber: "except to the extent" restores it  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST TRUE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): an "except" or "unless" read as re-including (the reader, JUST TRUE) versus a sentence that only lifts an exclusion or a bar and leaves the first sentence to decide (the encoder, NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(d) the information is a communication` WITH `the information is exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties` IS TRUE, `the information is exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 18. Art 2(d): group chat of 30 is a finite number of parties
#ASSERT (`Art 2(d) the information is a communication` WITH `the information is exchanged or conveyed between a finite number of parties` IS TRUE, `the information is exchanged or conveyed by means of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 19. Art 2(d): Guide: means definition; not by a publicly available service
#ASSERT (`Art 2(h) the message is electronic mail` WITH `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `the message is sent over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 20. Art 2(h): SMS
#ASSERT (`Art 2(h) the message is electronic mail` WITH `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `the message is sent over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 21. Art 2(h): Guide: means definition; live call not storable
#ASSERT (`Art 2(h) the message is electronic mail` WITH `the message is a text, voice, sound or image message` IS TRUE, `the message is sent over a public communications network` IS TRUE, `the message can be stored in the network or in the recipient's terminal equipment until it is collected by the recipient` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 22. Art 2(h): voicemail
#ASSERT (`Art 2(g) the service is a value added service` WITH `the service requires the processing of traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS FALSE, `the service requires the processing of location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 23. Art 2(g)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(g) the service is a value added service` WITH `the service requires the processing of traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS FALSE, `the service requires the processing of location data other than traffic data beyond what is necessary for the transmission of a communication or the billing thereof` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 24. Art 2(g): Guide: means definition
#ASSERT (`Art 2(i) the event is a personal data breach` WITH `the event is a breach of security` IS TRUE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data` IS TRUE, `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 25. Art 2(i)
#ASSERT (`Art 2(i) the event is a personal data breach` WITH `the event is a breach of security` IS TRUE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data` IS TRUE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data` IS FALSE, `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 26. Art 2(i): lost backup tape
#ASSERT (`Art 2(i) the event is a personal data breach` WITH `the event is a breach of security` IS TRUE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data` IS TRUE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data` IS FALSE, `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 27. Art 2(i): Guide: means definition; data not in connection with the service
#ASSERT (`Art 2(i) the event is a personal data breach` WITH `the event is a breach of security` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful destruction of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful loss of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the accidental or unlawful alteration of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to the unauthorised disclosure of the data` IS FALSE, `the breach leads to unauthorised access to the data` IS TRUE, `the data is personal data transmitted, stored or otherwise processed in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 28. Art 2(i): Guide: means definition; no breach of security
#ASSERT (`Art 2 the paragraph of this Directive that defines the term` WITH term IS `subscriber`) EQUALS NOTHING -- 29. Art 2 chapeau: Guide: term defined outside the sources
#ASSERT (`Art 3 the Directive applies to the processing` WITH `the processing is of personal data` IS TRUE, `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE, `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices` IS TRUE, `the network is in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 31. Art 3
#ASSERT (`Art 3 the Directive applies to the processing` WITH `the processing is of personal data` IS TRUE, `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE, `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices` IS TRUE, `the network is in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 32. Art 3: network supporting data collection and identification devices: "including"
#ASSERT (`Art 3 the Directive applies to the processing` WITH `the processing is of personal data` IS TRUE, `the processing is in connection with the provision of a publicly available electronic communications service` IS TRUE, `the network is a public communications network, including a public communications network supporting data collection and identification devices` IS FALSE, `the network is in the Community` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 33. Art 3: Guide: scope limit with no only (ruling (c)); private corporate network
#ASSERT (`Art 4(1) first sentence the provider's duty to take appropriate measures is met` WITH `the provider has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the security of its services` IS TRUE, `acting in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network is necessary with respect to network security` IS FALSE, `the provider has acted in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 34. Art 4(1)
#ASSERT (`Art 4(1) first sentence the provider's duty to take appropriate measures is met` WITH `the provider has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the security of its services` IS FALSE, `acting in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network is necessary with respect to network security` IS FALSE, `the provider has acted in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 35. Art 4(1): CB: bare must not done
#ASSERT (`Art 4(1a) the measures include at least what the three dashes require` WITH `the measures ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes` IS TRUE, `the measures protect personal data stored or transmitted against accidental or unlawful destruction, accidental loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure` IS TRUE, `the measures ensure the implementation of a security policy with respect to the processing of personal data` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 36. Art 4(1a)
#ASSERT (`Art 4(1a) the measures include at least what the three dashes require` WITH `the measures ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes` IS TRUE, `the measures protect personal data stored or transmitted against accidental or unlawful destruction, accidental loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure` IS TRUE, `the measures ensure the implementation of a security policy with respect to the processing of personal data` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 37. Art 4(1a): shall at least; no security policy
#ASSERT (`Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers concerning the risk` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 38. Art 4(2): risk within the provider own measures
#ASSERT (`Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers of any possible remedies, including the likely costs` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE, `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 39. Art 4(2): Guide: where condition fails (ruling (b)); risk within own measures
#ASSERT (`Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers of any possible remedies, including the likely costs` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS TRUE, `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 40. Art 4(2)
#ASSERT (`Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers concerning the risk` WITH `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 41. Art 4(2): Guide: "in case of" is an if
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider must notify the competent national authority` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 42. Art 4(3) first subparagraph: whether or not anyone is likely to be harmed
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider must also notify the subscriber or individual` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 43. Art 4(3) second subparagraph: Guide: "when" counts as "where" (ruling (c))
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider must also notify the subscriber or individual` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 44. Art 4(3) second subparagraph
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS TRUE, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS TRUE, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 45. Art 4(3) third subparagraph: Guide: flat negative "shall not be required if"
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS FALSE, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS TRUE, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 46. Art 4(3) third subparagraph: protection not demonstrated to the authority: exemption not met, so the second subparagraph requires the notification  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST TRUE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): "shall not be required if" with the "if" unmet is silent (NOTHING, the encoder) versus required (JUST TRUE, the reader)
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` WITH `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS TRUE, `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS FALSE, `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 47. Art 4(3) third subparagraph: protection not applied to the data concerned: exemption not met, so notification required  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST TRUE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): "shall not be required if" with the "if" unmet is silent (NOTHING, the encoder) versus required (JUST TRUE, the reader)
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider must notify the competent national authority` WITH `there has been a personal data breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 48. Art 4(3) first subparagraph: the exemption of 45 concerns the subscriber only; the authority must still be notified
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph the competent national authority may require the provider to notify the subscriber or individual` WITH `the provider has not already notified the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the competent national authority has considered the likely adverse effects of the breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 49. Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph the competent national authority may require the provider to notify the subscriber or individual` WITH `the provider has not already notified the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach` IS FALSE, `the competent national authority has considered the likely adverse effects of the breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 50. Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph: Guide: the text introduces the condition with "if" (worked example 1); provider already notified  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST FALSE; SCENARIO (the lead's prompt defect, not an encoder fault): a function named for a power ("may") whose "if" gate failed answers NOTHING under the Guide's grant-and-power ruling (2026-11-12), limit 1, and the text does not close the gate with "only"; the reader's expectation came from a worked example in the lead's prompt that contradicted that ruling; encoder fork F13
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual has the content required` WITH `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS TRUE, `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 51. Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual has the content required` WITH `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS TRUE, `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 52. Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph: shall at least; no recommended measures
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the competent national authority has the content required` WITH `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS TRUE, `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the consequences of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address the personal data breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 53. Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph
#ASSERT (`Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the competent national authority has the content required` WITH `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS TRUE, `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS TRUE, `the notification describes the consequences of the personal data breach` IS FALSE, `the notification describes the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address the personal data breach` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 54. Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph: in addition: no consequences
#ASSERT (`Art 4(4) second subparagraph the provider's inventory of personal data breaches is as required` WITH `the inventory comprises the facts surrounding the breach` IS TRUE, `the inventory comprises the effects of the breach` IS TRUE, `the inventory comprises the remedial action taken` IS TRUE, `the inventory is sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3` IS TRUE, `the inventory includes only the information necessary for this purpose` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 55. Art 4(4) second subparagraph
#ASSERT (`Art 4(4) second subparagraph the provider's inventory of personal data breaches is as required` WITH `the inventory comprises the facts surrounding the breach` IS TRUE, `the inventory comprises the effects of the breach` IS TRUE, `the inventory comprises the remedial action taken` IS FALSE, `the inventory is sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3` IS TRUE, `the inventory includes only the information necessary for this purpose` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 56. Art 4(4) second subparagraph: no remedial action
#ASSERT (`Art 4(4) second subparagraph the provider's inventory of personal data breaches is as required` WITH `the inventory comprises the facts surrounding the breach` IS TRUE, `the inventory comprises the effects of the breach` IS TRUE, `the inventory comprises the remedial action taken` IS TRUE, `the inventory is sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3` IS TRUE, `the inventory includes only the information necessary for this purpose` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 57. Art 4(4) second subparagraph: Guide: "shall only include"; includes unnecessary information
#ASSERT (`Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority must impose appropriate sanctions on the provider` WITH `the provider has failed to comply with its notification obligations` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 58. Art 4(4) first subparagraph
#ASSERT (`Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` WITH `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the act is by a person other than a user` IS TRUE, `the users concerned have consented` IS FALSE, `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 60. Art 5(1)
#ASSERT (`Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` WITH `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the act is by a person other than a user` IS TRUE, `the users concerned have consented` IS TRUE, `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 61. Art 5(1): prohibition is "without the consent of the users concerned"; with consent it does not bite  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST FALSE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): "without the consent" / "without prejudice to" read like "unless" (the reader, JUST FALSE) versus a limit on the prohibition in its own wording (the encoder, NOTHING)
#ASSERT (`Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` WITH `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the act is by a person other than a user` IS TRUE, `the users concerned have consented` IS FALSE, `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 62. Art 5(1): CB: "except" once met
#ASSERT (`Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` WITH `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS TRUE, `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the act is by a person other than a user` IS FALSE, `the users concerned have consented` IS FALSE, `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 63. Art 5(1): Guide: prohibition limited to persons other than users; a user is outside the limit
#ASSERT (`Art 5(1) third sentence the paragraph prevents the storage` WITH `the storage is technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication` IS TRUE, `the storage is without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 64. Art 5(1) third sentence: Guide: flat negative "shall not prevent"
#ASSERT (`Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS TRUE, `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` IS TRUE, `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 65. Art 5(2): Guide: flat negative "shall not affect"
#ASSERT (`Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` WITH `the recording is legally authorised` IS TRUE, `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` IS TRUE, `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` IS TRUE, `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING -- 66. Art 5(2): Guide: limited by its own wording; recording for a marketing profile
#ASSERT (`Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` WITH `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS TRUE, `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS TRUE, `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 67. Art 5(3): condition met
#ASSERT (`Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` WITH `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS FALSE, `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS FALSE, `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 68. Art 5(3): Guide: "only ... on condition"; no consent (exemption not asked here, see GAP note)
#ASSERT (`Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` WITH `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS TRUE, `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS FALSE, `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 69. Art 5(3): Guide: "only ... on condition"; consent without clear and comprehensive information
#ASSERT (`Art 5(3) second sentence the first sentence prevents the storage or access` WITH `it is technical storage or access` IS TRUE, `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network` IS TRUE, `the provider of an information society service was explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service` IS FALSE, `the storage or access is strictly necessary in order for that provider to provide the service` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 70. Art 5(3) second sentence: Guide: flat negative "shall not prevent": sole purpose of transmission is allowed, so the consent rule does not prevent it
#ASSERT (`Art 5(3) second sentence the first sentence prevents the storage or access` WITH `it is technical storage or access` IS TRUE, `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network` IS FALSE, `the provider of an information society service was explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service` IS TRUE, `the storage or access is strictly necessary in order for that provider to provide the service` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- 71. Art 5(3) second sentence: Guide: flat negative "shall not prevent": strictly necessary for an explicitly requested service
