#ASSERT (`Must national law make an unsolicited marketing call that is not an automatic call fax or e-mail not allowed` WITH `the call or message reached me by` IS `another means of communication`, `I did not ask for it` IS TRUE, `it is for direct marketing` IS TRUE, `national law has chosen` IS `national legislation has not been stated`, `I gave my consent` IS FALSE, `I do not wish to receive them` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- 291. Art 13(3) [individual seat]: extra: no consent and I have said I do not wish to receive them: both national options protect me, so national law must stop it whichever option it chose (seat answer JUST TRUE = must stop)  -- RENAMED (lead, 2026-11-18): the encoder re-worded this seat question as a yes/no after an independent polarity pass; JUST TRUE = yes, national law must make it not allowed; the expectation is unchanged
