-- GAPS (scenarios the encoding cannot be asked; no assertion written):
-- GAP 30. Art 2(f): no function judges whether an act is valid consent under Directive 95/46/EC: the encoding takes that as a plain yes/no input (Art 2(f) function returns what it is told)
-- GAP 46-47 composite. Art 4(3) second and third subparagraphs: no function composes the duty to notify the subscriber (second subparagraph) with the exemption (third subparagraph): "is notification to the subscriber required on these facts" needs both and only the pieces exist
-- GAP 59. Art 4(5): not encoded: the Commission power to adopt technical implementing measures is declared inert machinery
-- GAP 72-75 composite. Art 5(3): no function composes the consent condition with the exemption into "may this be stored or read": only the two pieces exist, so "allowed? NO" for a non-exempt unconsented cookie cannot be asked in one call
-- GAP 81. Art 6(1): no boolean "duty is met" function for 6(1): only a regulative rule whose single act is "erase or make anonymous", so the alternative (anonymised instead of erased) is not an input
-- GAP 90. Art 6(3) second sentence: no function takes "the provider gives no possibility to withdraw": the only function takes whether consent was given, so non-compliance cannot be asked
-- GAP 99. Art 7(2): no compliance function: the encoding answers only whether the Member State duty binds, not whether a Member State complied
-- GAP 110. Art 8(3): no input for a charge on the rejection feature: the duty function takes only offers and simple means, so "may the provider charge a fee" (silent: NOTHING) cannot be asked
-- GAP 145. Art 12(2) second sentence: no input for a charge on being INCLUDED in the directory: the function asks only whether non-inclusion, verifying, correcting and withdrawing were free, so the silent case (NOTHING) cannot be asked
-- GAP 200. Art 14a(1): not encoded: the committee procedure is declared inert machinery
-- GAP 220. Art 15a(4) second subparagraph: not encoded: the duty to give the Commission a summary in good time is declared inert machinery
-- GAP 221. Art 15a(4) second subparagraph: not encoded: same
